## Api Shops Photos By Slug [/api/shops/{slug}/photos]

+ Parameters
    + slug (string, required)

        The shop's link name (current or former).

        + Sample: raptorrush

### addPhotos [POST]
Adds one or more photos after the cover. Each is turned upright, resized to at most 2000 px and stored as WebP. A shop holds up to 8 photos; buyers swipe through them on the shop page. Not for recommendations, which show the retailer's photos.
+ Attributes
    + photo (string, required)

        An image, up to 15 MB. The endpoint also accepts the field repeated, to add several in one request.


+ Request (multipart/form-data)




+ Response 200 (application/json)

        The shop's photos, cover first.

    + Attributes (ShopPhotos)


    + Body

            {"photos":[{"id":"LFRvGuTU3D8i334X","url":"/api/blobs/LFRvGuTU3D8i334X"},{"id":"zrySajNyao6_j11x","url":"/api/blobs/zrySajNyao6_j11x"}]}


+ Response 400 (application/json)

        Something in the request needs fixing; `error` says what.

    + Attributes (Error)


    + Body

            {"error":"Choose a photo."}


+ Response 404 (application/json)

        No such shop, or the admin token or API key doesn't match it.

    + Attributes (Error)


    + Body

            {"error":"Shop not found."}


### setPhotoOrder [PUT]
Sets the photo order; the first becomes the cover. Leaving a photo out removes it.

