## Api Shops Suggest By Slug [/api/shops/{slug}/suggest]

+ Parameters
    + slug (string, required)

        The shop's link name (current or former).

        + Sample: raptorrush

### checkMissingDetails [POST]
Asks Gemini what buyers will want to choose (sizes, colours) and what they'll ask that the
listing doesn't say (dimensions, materials). `createShop` already does this once; call it
again after editing the product. The result is saved as the shop's `suggestions`.

Nothing changes on the shop page until the seller confirms: save options with `updateShop`
(`options`), and answer the questions with `updateShop` (`facts`). Not for recommendations.

+ Response 200 (application/json)

        The suggestions.

    + Attributes (Suggestions)


    + Body

            {"oneOfAKind":false,"options":[{"name":"Size","kind":"size","values":[{"label":"7"},{"label":"8"},{"label":"9"}],"fromSeller":false}],"missingFacts":[{"label":"Wheel size","question":"How big are the wheels?","placeholder":"57 mm"}]}


+ Response 400 (application/json)

        Something in the request needs fixing; `error` says what.

    + Attributes (Error)


    + Body

            {"error":"Choose a photo."}


+ Response 404 (application/json)

        No such shop, or the admin token or API key doesn't match it.

    + Attributes (Error)


    + Body

            {"error":"Shop not found."}


+ Response 502 (application/json)

        Gemini, PayPal or Channel3 failed or isn't configured.

    + Attributes (Error)


    + Body

            {"error":"PayPal isn't configured on this server."}


+ Response 429 (application/json)

        Over this network's cap for the call (see **Limits**). Retry after `Retry-After` seconds.

    + Attributes (Error)


    + Body

            {"error":"Too many checkouts from your network. Try again in 7 min."}



