## Api Shops Paypal By Slug [/api/shops/{slug}/paypal]

+ Parameters
    + slug (string, required)

        The shop's link name (current or former).

        + Sample: raptorrush

### connectPayPal [POST]
Starts PayPal's seller onboarding (Partner Referrals). Send the seller's browser to the
returned `url`; they sign in to PayPal (or create a business account) and grant OneThing
permission. PayPal brings them back to `/api/shops/<slug>/paypal/return`, which saves the
connection and opens the manage page. From then on, sales are paid to that account.

Without a connection, a shop can still go live with a typed `paypal_email`.

**Platforms:** call it with your API key and a `returnUrl`, and PayPal's flow ends on your own
page instead, as `returnUrl?paypal=connected|incomplete|cancelled|failed&shop=<slug>`. The
URL's origin must be one registered on the key.

+ Request (<<Add Header Value>>)

    + Attributes (Api Shops Paypal Request)


    + Body

            {
                "returnUrl": "https://www.miriogames.com/market/manage/?g=7Hq2"
            }


+ Response 200 (application/json)

        Where to send the seller.

    + Attributes (Api Shops Paypal Response)


    + Body

            {"url":"https://www.sandbox.paypal.com/bizsignup/partner/entry?referralToken=EXAMPLE"}


+ Response 404 (application/json)

        No such shop, or the admin token or API key doesn't match it.

    + Attributes (Error)


    + Body

            {"error":"Shop not found."}


+ Response 502 (application/json)

        Gemini, PayPal or Channel3 failed or isn't configured.

    + Attributes (Error)


    + Body

            {"error":"PayPal isn't configured on this server."}


+ Response 503 (application/json)

        Gemini, PayPal or Channel3 failed or isn't configured.

    + Attributes (Error)


    + Body

            {"error":"PayPal isn't configured on this server."}


### getPayPalConnection [GET]
Asks PayPal where the seller's connection stands and saves it on the shop. Also finds a connection the seller finished at PayPal without coming back.

+ Response 200 (application/json)

        The connection, or nulls if there is none yet.

    + Attributes (Api Shops Paypal Response1)


    + Body

            {"merchantId":"7MZJ4QXN8K2LA","status":{"receivable":true,"emailConfirmed":true,"checkedAt":"2026-10-21T18:04:11Z"}}


+ Response 404 (application/json)

        No such shop, or the admin token or API key doesn't match it.

    + Attributes (Error)


    + Body

            {"error":"Shop not found."}


+ Response 502 (application/json)

        Gemini, PayPal or Channel3 failed or isn't configured.

    + Attributes (Error)


    + Body

            {"error":"PayPal isn't configured on this server."}


+ Response 503 (application/json)

        Gemini, PayPal or Channel3 failed or isn't configured.

    + Attributes (Error)


    + Body

            {"error":"PayPal isn't configured on this server."}


### disconnectPayPal [DELETE]
Forgets the connected account. Sales go back to the shop's `paypal_email`.

+ Response 200 (application/json)

        Done.

    + Attributes (Ok)


    + Body

            {"ok":true}


+ Response 404 (application/json)

        No such shop, or the admin token or API key doesn't match it.

    + Attributes (Error)


    + Body

            {"error":"Shop not found."}




# Group Links

Short shop links (`/<slug>`).

## Api Slugs Check [/api/slugs/check{?name}]

### checkLinkName [GET]
Normalises a proposed link name and says whether a new shop can use it.
+ Parameters
    + name (string, required)

        Anything; it is normalised (`Raptor Rush` becomes `raptor-rush`).

        + Sample: Raptor Rush

+ Response 200 (application/json)

        The normalised name and whether it can be used.

    + Attributes (Api Slugs Check Response)


    + Body

            {"slug":"raptor-rush","available":true}




# Group Products

Find products to recommend (Channel3 catalog).

## Api Channel3 Search [/api/channel3/search{?q}]

### searchProducts [GET]
Searches 100M+ products from 25k+ stores through Channel3. Pass a result's `id` to `createShop` with `source=channel3`.
+ Parameters
    + q (string, required)

        What to look for, in plain words.

        + Sample: gifts for trail runners under $60

+ Response 200 (application/json)

        Up to 12 products.

