# Group Agents

Machine-readable shops and the MCP server AI shopping agents buy through.

## O By OrderId [/o/{orderId}]

+ Parameters
    + orderId (string, required)

        The `order_id` from the MCP `create_order` tool.

        + Sample: pX4kR9tVb2nQ7sLe

### openPayLink [GET]
The `pay_url` an agent gives the buyer. It redirects to PayPal's payment page for the order, so PayPal's checkout token never passes through the agent (agent platforms hide such tokens as secrets). A paid order redirects to its thank-you page; an expired checkout goes back to the shop page.

+ Response 303 

        Redirect to PayPal, the thank-you page or the shop page.




+ Response 404 (text/plain)

        No order with that id.

    + Attributes (string)




## Api Agent Shops [/api/agent/shops{?q,limit}]

### listAgentShops [GET]
The gallery's live shops for a query: shops matching more of its words first, newest first among equals. Browsing words ("something interesting to buy") are ignored, and a query that matches nothing returns the newest shops with `matched: false` rather than an empty list. The GET twin of the MCP `search_shops` tool, for agents that can only fetch URLs. Public. Read a shop with `getAgentProduct`; buy through the MCP server in `mcp_server`, or send the buyer to the shop's `url`.
+ Parameters
    + q (string, optional)

        Keywords. Leave out to list the newest shops.

        + Sample: skates
    + limit (number, optional) -

        How many shops, 1–25.

        + Default: 10
        + Sample: 10

+ Response 200 (application/json)

        The matching shops.

    + Attributes (Api Agent Shops Response)


    + Body

            {"show_buyer":"![Vintage Cream and Red Roller Skates](https://one-thing-ash0.onrender.com/api/blobs/LFRvGuTU3D8i334X)\n\n**Vintage Cream and Red Roller Skates**: $240.00. Classic quad skates crafted with walnut burl heels\n\n![Raptor Rush: Browser Edition](https://one-thing-ash0.onrender.com/api/blobs/R9tWc3yN6bJq1zUd)\n\n**Raptor Rush: Browser Edition**: $2.99. Grow from Tiny Hatchling to Giant Apex Predator\n\nWhich one?","shops":[{"shop":"vintageskates","name":"Vintage Cream and Red Roller Skates","kind":"physical","headline":"Classic quad skates crafted with walnut burl heels","price":"$240.00","image":"https://one-thing-ash0.onrender.com/api/blobs/LFRvGuTU3D8i334X","url":"https://one-thing-ash0.onrender.com/vintageskates"},{"shop":"raptorrush","name":"Raptor Rush: Browser Edition","kind":"digital","headline":"Grow from Tiny Hatchling to Giant Apex Predator","price":"$2.99","image":"https://one-thing-ash0.onrender.com/api/blobs/R9tWc3yN6bJq1zUd","url":"https://one-thing-ash0.onrender.com/raptorrush"}],"matched":true,"mcp_server":"https://one-thing-ash0.onrender.com/api/mcp"}



## Api Agent Shops Order By Slug [/api/agent/shops/{slug}/order{?agent,Size}]

+ Parameters
    + slug (string, required)

        The shop's link name (current or former).

        + Sample: raptorrush

### orderByLink [GET]
Orders one unit with a GET: the MCP `create_order` tool for AI assistants that can only
fetch URLs, such as free-tier ChatGPT or Grok. Nothing is charged. The reply has `pay_url`,
where the buyer pays at PayPal, and `status_url` (`getAgentOrder`), which says when they
have and what they got.

For a product with options, pass the buyer's pick as query parameters named after the
options (`?Size=9`, or `?Color=Ice+Blue&Size=L`); names and values are matched without
regard to case. You rarely build this URL yourself: `getAgentProduct` and `/llms.txt`
write it out in full (`order_url`, or `variants[].order_url`), because some assistants
only open URLs they have been shown.

Every request makes a new order, so open it once, after the buyer says to buy. Known
crawlers and link previewers get a 403 (and are kept out by `robots.txt`); any other
leaves an unpaid order at most, since stock is only taken when a payment is captured.
Replies are `no-store` and `X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow`.

`/<slug>/buy` is the same endpoint at a short URL, and the one `order_url` uses.
A person clicking the link in a browser (`Sec-Fetch-User: ?1`) is redirected instead; known assistants and headless browsers always get JSON. It goes straight to `pay_url`, or to the shop page when an option is missing
or unknown.
+ Parameters
    + agent (string, optional)

        Optional: the agent's name (`ChatGPT`, `Gemini`, `my-shopping-bot`), so the seller's stats show which agent sent the buyer. Only used when the user agent doesn't already say.

        + Sample: ChatGPT
    + Size (string, optional)

        An example option. The real parameter names are the product's option names from `getAgentProduct` (`options[].name`), one per option.

        + Sample: 9

+ Response 200 (application/json)

        The order, waiting for the buyer to pay.

    + Attributes (AgentCreatedOrder)


    + Body

            {"show_buyer":"![Vintage Cream and Red Roller Skates](https://one-thing-ash0.onrender.com/api/blobs/LFRvGuTU3D8i334X)\n\nVintage Cream and Red Roller Skates (9): $255.00 total.\n**[Pay $255.00 with PayPal](https://one-thing-ash0.onrender.com/o/pX4kR9tVb2nQ7sLe)**\nTell me once you've paid and I'll get you the shipping confirmation.","order_id":"pX4kR9tVb2nQ7sLe","status":"awaiting_buyer_approval","total":"$255.00","options":{"Size":"9"},"pay_url":"https://one-thing-ash0.onrender.com/o/pX4kR9tVb2nQ7sLe","status_url":"https://one-thing-ash0.onrender.com/o/pX4kR9tVb2nQ7sLe/status","next_step":"Show pay_url to the buyer as a link. It opens PayPal, where they pay (and enter a shipping address for physical items). When they say they've paid, open status_url (or with MCP, call get_order with order_id): it returns the access code, download link or shipping details."}


+ Response 303 

        A person clicked the link. Redirect to PayPal (`pay_url`), or to the shop page to pick an option.




+ Response 400 (application/json)

        A missing or unknown option value, or sold out. `error` names the valid values.

    + Attributes (Error)


    + Body

            {"error":"Unknown Size \"12\". Size: one of 7, 8, 9."}


+ Response 403 (application/json)

        A known crawler or link previewer. They don't place orders.

    + Attributes (Error)


    + Body

            {"error":"Crawlers and link previews don't place orders. Read the product at the shop's page."}


+ Response 404 (application/json)

        No live shop with that link name.

    + Attributes (Error)


    + Body

            {"error":"No live shop called \"skatez\". Try search_shops."}


+ Response 429 (application/json)

        Over this network's cap for the call (see **Limits**). Retry after `Retry-After` seconds.

    + Attributes (Error)


    + Body

            {"error":"Too many checkouts from your network. Try again in 7 min."}



## Api Agent Orders By OrderId [/api/agent/orders/{orderId}{?agent}]

+ Parameters
    + orderId (string, required)

        The `order_id` from the MCP `create_order` tool, or from a thank-you page link (`?order=`).

        + Sample: pX4kR9tVb2nQ7sLe

### getAgentOrder [GET]
Where an order stands and, once paid, what the buyer got: the access code, the download link, or the shipping address and tracking. The GET twin of the MCP `get_order` tool (and the `status_url` that `create_order` returns), for agents that can only fetch URLs. Public: anyone with the order id can already open its thank-you page. If the buyer has approved at PayPal but nothing has captured the payment yet, this captures it. `/o/<order_id>/status` is the same endpoint at a short URL, and the one `status_url` uses. A person clicking the link in a browser (`Sec-Fetch-User: ?1`) is redirected instead; known assistants and headless browsers always get JSON. It goes to the order's receipt page.
+ Parameters
    + agent (string, optional)

        Optional: the agent's name (`ChatGPT`, `Gemini`, `my-shopping-bot`), so the seller's stats show which agent sent the buyer. Only used when the user agent doesn't already say.

        + Sample: ChatGPT

+ Response 200 (application/json)

        The order.

    + Attributes (AgentOrder)


    + Body

            {"order_id":"pX4kR9tVb2nQ7sLe","status":"awaiting_buyer_approval","product":"Vintage Cream and Red Roller Skates","options":{"Size":"9"},"amount":{"item":240,"shipping":15,"total":255,"currency":"USD"},"total":"$255.00","pay_url":"https://one-thing-ash0.onrender.com/o/pX4kR9tVb2nQ7sLe","next_step":"The buyer hasn't paid yet. Give them pay_url; when they say they've paid, call get_order again."}


+ Response 303 

        A person clicked the link. Redirect to the order's page (`/o/<order_id>`).




+ Response 404 (application/json)

        No order with that id.

    + Attributes (Error)




## Api Agent Shops By Slug [/api/agent/shops/{slug}{?agent,view}]

+ Parameters
    + slug (string, required)

        The shop's link name (current or former).

        + Sample: raptorrush

### getAgentProduct [GET]
Everything an AI shopping agent needs to describe the product and decide to buy it: price, shipping, delivery, availability, options, images and FAQ. Public. Buying goes through the MCP server named in `mcp_server`, or the `order_url` links. Shop pages also carry the same facts as schema.org `Product` JSON-LD. A person clicking the link in a browser (`Sec-Fetch-User: ?1`) is redirected instead; known assistants and headless browsers always get JSON. It goes to the shop page, unless the link has `?view=json`.
+ Parameters
    + agent (string, optional)

        Optional: the agent's name (`ChatGPT`, `Gemini`, `my-shopping-bot`), so the seller's stats show which agent sent the buyer. Only used when the user agent doesn't already say.

        + Sample: ChatGPT
    + view (enum[string], optional)

        `json` keeps the JSON for a person opening the link in a browser.

        + Sample: json
        + Members
            + `json` 


+ Response 200 (application/json)

        The product.

    + Attributes (AgentProduct)


    + Body

            {"show_buyer":"![Vintage Cream and Red Roller Skates](https://one-thing-ash0.onrender.com/api/blobs/LFRvGuTU3D8i334X)\n\n**Vintage Cream and Red Roller Skates**: $240.00 + $15.00 shipping\nClassic quad skates crafted with walnut burl heels\nSize: 7 · 8 · 9\nWhich size?","shop":"vintageskates","url":"https://one-thing-ash0.onrender.com/vintageskates","name":"Vintage Cream and Red Roller Skates","kind":"physical","headline":"Classic quad skates crafted with walnut burl heels","description":"A vintage pair of skates featuring cream leather, bold red trim, and durable quad wheels.","highlights":["Handmade cream leather upper with rich red trim","Sculpted walnut burl heel structure for stability"],"details":[{"label":"Materials","value":"Leather upper, walnut burl heel, rubber wheels"}],"faq":[{"q":"What is the return policy?","a":"Unworn skates in original condition can be returned within 30 days of delivery."}],"images":["https://one-thing-ash0.onrender.com/api/blobs/LFRvGuTU3D8i334X","https://one-thing-ash0.onrender.com/api/blobs/zrySajNyao6_j11x"],"price":{"amount":240,"currency":"USD","label":"$240.00"},"shipping":{"amount":15,"currency":"USD","ships_to":["US"]},"total":{"amount":255,"currency":"USD"},"delivery":"Shipped. PayPal collects the buyer's address at checkout.","options":[{"name":"Size","values":["7","8","9"]}],"variants":[{"choice":{"Size":"7"},"availability":"in_stock (3 left)","order_url":"https://one-thing-ash0.onrender.com/vintageskates/buy?Size=7"},{"choice":{"Size":"8"},"availability":"sold_out"},{"choice":{"Size":"9"},"availability":"in_stock (6 left)","order_url":"https://one-thing-ash0.onrender.com/vintageskates/buy?Size=9"}],"availability":"in_stock","how_to_buy":"Show show_buyer to the buyer exactly as written, photo included (it's Markdown, so the photo displays and the links stay clickable), and keep your own words to a minimum. Once the buyer has picked and said to buy, open the order_url of their variant (or call create_order on the OneThing MCP server with shop and options). Either returns show_buyer with the pay link.","mcp_server":"https://one-thing-ash0.onrender.com/api/mcp","agent_name":"ChatGPT"}


+ Response 303 

        A person clicked the link. Redirect to the shop page (`/<slug>`).




+ Response 404 (application/json)

        No live shop with that link name.

    + Attributes (Error)




## Api Mcp [/api/mcp]

### callMcp [POST]
A [Model Context Protocol](https://modelcontextprotocol.io) server, so agents such as
Claude can shop here. Add `https://<host>/api/mcp` to an MCP client as a Streamable HTTP
server. It's stateless: each POST carries one JSON-RPC 2.0 message (or a batch) and gets a
plain JSON reply, with no event stream. The `initialize` reply's `Mcp-Session-Id` header
carries the client's `clientInfo.name`; send it back on later requests (MCP clients do)
so the seller's stats show which agent sent the buyer. Nothing else is kept.

Methods: `initialize`, `ping`, `tools/list`, `tools/call`, and `resources/list`,
`resources/templates/list` and `resources/read` for the product card. Each tool carries
`annotations` (only `create_order` isn't `readOnlyHint`). Tools:

| Tool | Arguments | What it does |
|---|---|---|
| `search_shops` | `query?`, `limit?` (1–25) | Live gallery shops, best match first; no match returns the newest with `matched: false` |
| `get_product` | `shop` | The same object as `getAgentProduct` |
| `create_order` | `shop`, `options?` | One unit on order; returns `order_id` and `pay_url` |
| `get_order` | `order_id` | Status and `next_step`; once paid, the receipt and `delivery` |

**The buyer always approves.** `create_order` charges nothing: the agent shows the buyer
`pay_url` (`/o/<order_id>`, see `openPayLink`), which opens PayPal. It's a plain link on this
site, so agent platforms that hide PayPal's checkout tokens can still show it. When the buyer
says they've paid, the agent calls `get_order`.

`get_order` status is one of `awaiting_buyer_approval`, `paid`, `declined` (nothing charged;
the buyer can open `pay_url` again), `sold_out`, `expired` (call `create_order` again) or
`failed` (PayPal couldn't be reached; try again), with a `next_step` the agent can follow.
A paid order carries `delivery`: `{type: access_code, access_code, start_url?}`,
`{type: download, download_url}` or `{type: shipping, ship_to, fulfillment, tracking}`, plus
`amount` with item, shipping and total. Orders made this way show `channel: agent` in
`listOrders`.

**The product card.** Hosts that draw MCP Apps UI (ChatGPT, or a client that declares the
`io.modelcontextprotocol/ui` extension) get `search_shops`, `get_product` and
`create_order` results as a card with the real photos, options and a Pay with PayPal button
(`ui://onething/shop-card-v1.html`). For them `show_buyer` is a one-line note rather than
Markdown, so the model doesn't repeat or invent what the card shows.

Tool errors (an unknown shop, a sold-out size, over the checkout cap) come back as results
with `isError: true`, so the model can read them and try something else.

+ Request (<<Add Header Value>>)

    + Attributes (string)


    + Body

            {
                "jsonrpc": "2.0",
                "id": 1,
                "method": "tools/call",
                "params": {
                    "name": "search_shops",
                    "arguments": {
                        "query": "game"
                    }
                }
            }


+ Response 200 (application/json)

        The JSON-RPC reply (an array for a batch).

    + Attributes (string)


    + Body

            {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"show_buyer\": \"![Vintage Cream and Red Roller Skates](https://one-thing-ash0.onrender.com/api/blobs/LFRvGuTU3D8i334X)\\n\\n**Vintage Cream and Red Roller Skates**: $240.00. Classic quad skates crafted with walnut burl heels\\n\\nWant it?\",\n  \"shops\": [\n    {\n      \"shop\": \"vintageskates\",\n      \"name\": \"Vintage Cream and Red Roller Skates\",\n      \"kind\": \"physical\",\n      \"headline\": \"Classic quad skates crafted with walnut burl heels\",\n      \"price\": \"$240.00\",\n      \"image\": \"https://one-thing-ash0.onrender.com/api/blobs/LFRvGuTU3D8i334X\",\n      \"url\": \"https://one-thing-ash0.onrender.com/vintageskates\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"agent_name\": \"Claude\"\n}"}],"structuredContent":{"show_buyer":"![Vintage Cream and Red Roller Skates](https://one-thing-ash0.onrender.com/api/blobs/LFRvGuTU3D8i334X)\n\n**Vintage Cream and Red Roller Skates**: $240.00. Classic quad skates crafted with walnut burl heels\n\nWant it?","shops":[{"shop":"vintageskates","name":"Vintage Cream and Red Roller Skates","kind":"physical","headline":"Classic quad skates crafted with walnut burl heels","price":"$240.00","image":"https://one-thing-ash0.onrender.com/api/blobs/LFRvGuTU3D8i334X","url":"https://one-thing-ash0.onrender.com/vintageskates"}],"agent_name":"Claude"},"isError":false}}


+ Response 202 

        Only notifications were sent; there's nothing to reply.




+ Response 400 (application/json)

        Not JSON (JSON-RPC parse error `-32700`).

    + Attributes (JsonRpcResponse)





# Group Platforms

For marketplaces that make and run shops for their own sellers with one API key.

## Api Platform Shops [/api/platform/shops{?status}]

### listMyShops [GET]
Every shop the API key's account owns, newest first, with what a catalog page needs: name, price, cover, link, whether PayPal is connected and how many sales it has.
+ Parameters
    + status (enum[string], optional)

        Only shops with this status, e.g. `live` for a public catalog.

        + Sample: live
        + Members
            + `draft` 
            + `live` 


+ Response 200 (application/json)

        The shops.

    + Attributes (Api Platform Shops Response)


    + Body

            {"shops":[{"slug":"raptorrush","status":"live","name":"Raptor Rush: Browser Edition","headline":"Grow from Tiny Hatchling to Giant Apex Predator","product_type":"digital","price":{"amount":2.99,"currency":"USD"},"url":"https://one-thing-ash0.onrender.com/raptorrush","cover":"https://one-thing-ash0.onrender.com/api/blobs/KchAi9jwZzo76SKh","paypal_connected":true,"sales":12,"created_at":"2026-10-12T20:31:44Z"}]}


+ Response 401 (application/json)

        No API key, or it's wrong or revoked.

    + Attributes (Error)





# Data Structures

## Error (object)


### Properties
+ `error` (string, required) - A sentence you can show to a person.
+ `field` (string, optional) - The form field at fault, when there is one.
+ `detail` (string, optional) - The upstream service's own message, for debugging.


## CreateShopForm (object)


### Properties
+ `source` (enum[string], required) 
    + `photo`
    + `link`
    + `channel3`
+ `photo` (string, optional) - `source=photo`: the product photo, up to 8 MB.
+ `description` (string, optional) - `source=photo`: a sentence or two about the product. Required if there is no photo.
+ `url` (string, optional) - `source=link`: a product page, or your own app or game page.
+ `productId` (string, optional) - `source=channel3`: a product id from `searchProducts`.
+ `slug` (string, optional) - The link name you want. If omitted, the AI suggests one.
+ `type` (enum[string], optional) 
    + `auto`
    + `physical`
    + `digital`
+ `delivery` (enum[string], optional) - For digital products. If omitted, the AI guesses.
    + `file`
    + `access_code`
+ `access_url` (string, optional) - Where buyers use an access code.
+ `price` (number, optional) - USD. If omitted, the AI suggests a price.
+ `shipping` (number, optional) 
+ `stock` (number, optional) 
+ `ship_countries`: `US` (string, optional) 
+ `paypal_email` (string, optional) 
+ `seller_email` (string, optional) 
+ `digital_file` (string, optional) 


## CreatedShop (object)


### Properties
+ `slug`: `dragonflight` (string, required) 
+ `token` (string, required) - The admin token. Shown once; store it.
+ `manageUrl` (string, required) - The seller's private manage page (contains the token).


## ShopUpdate (object)


### Properties
+ `slug` (string, optional) 
+ `status` (enum[string], optional) 
    + `draft`
    + `live`
+ `product_type` (enum[string], optional) - `referral` only for shops created from Channel3.
    + `physical`
    + `digital`
    + `referral`
+ `price` (number, optional) 
+ `shipping` (number, optional) 
+ `stock` (number, optional, nullable) 
+ `ship_countries` (string, optional, nullable) 
+ `delivery` (enum[string], optional) 
    + `file`
    + `access_code`
+ `access_url` (string, optional, nullable) 
+ `paypal_email` (string, optional, nullable) 
+ `seller_email` (string, optional, nullable) 
+ `zapier_hook_url` (string, optional, nullable) 
+ `in_gallery` (boolean, optional) - Feature the shop at `/gallery` while it's live. Off by default.
+ `options` (array[ShopOption], optional) - What the buyer picks (physical products only), replacing the current options; `[]` removes them. With options, stock is counted per combination in `option_stock` and the shop's own `stock` is cleared. At most 60 combinations.
+ `option_stock`: `{"M / Black":4,"L / Black":0}` (number, optional) - Stock per combination, keyed by its values in option order joined with ` / ` (e.g. `M / Black`). A missing key or `null` means unlimited; `0` is sold out.
+ `facts` (array[Fact], optional) - Answers to the "buyers will ask" questions in `suggestions.missingFacts`. Each becomes a product detail on the page (replacing one with the same label) and drops off the list.


## Shop (object)


### Properties
+ `id` (string, required) 
+ `slug` (string, required) 
+ `status` (enum[string], required) 
    + `draft`
    + `live`
+ `product_type` (enum[string], required) 
    + `physical`
    + `digital`
    + `referral`
+ `price_cents` (number, required) 
+ `currency`: `USD` (string, required) 
+ `shipping_cents` (number, optional) 
+ `ship_countries` (string, optional, nullable) 
+ `stock` (number, optional, nullable) 
+ `delivery` (enum[string], optional) 
    + `file`
    + `access_code`
+ `access_url` (string, optional, nullable) 
+ `paypal_email` (string, optional, nullable) 
+ `seller_email` (string, optional, nullable) 
+ `paypal_merchant_id` (string, optional, nullable) - The connected PayPal account (`connectPayPal`). Sales go here when it can receive payments.
+ `paypal_status` (PayPalStatus, optional, nullable) 
+ `zapier_hook_url` (string, optional, nullable) 
+ `in_gallery` (boolean, optional) 
+ `account_id` (string, optional, nullable) - The seller account that owns the shop, if it was made while signed in.
+ `options` (array[ShopOption], optional) 
+ `option_stock`: `{"M / Black":4,"L / Black":0}` (number, optional) - Stock per combination, keyed by its values in option order joined with ` / ` (e.g. `M / Black`). A missing key or `null` means unlimited; `0` is sold out.
+ `suggestions` (Suggestions, optional, nullable) 
+ `photo_blob` (string, optional, nullable) - Image id for `getImage`. The cover photo.
+ `gallery_blobs` (array[string], optional) - The other photos, in order.
+ `hero_blob` (string, optional, nullable) 
+ `hero_status` (enum[string], optional) 
    + `none`
    + `pending`
    + `ready`
    + `failed`
+ `hero_error` (string, optional, nullable) 
+ `ai_source` (enum[string], optional) 
    + `gemini`
    + `fallback`
+ `source_url` (string, optional, nullable) 
+ `referral` (Referral, optional, nullable) 
+ `spec` (DesignSpec, required) - What Gemini designed. OneThing's templates render it; Gemini never writes HTML.
+ `created_at` (string, optional) 


## DesignSpec (object)
What Gemini designed. OneThing's templates render it; Gemini never writes HTML.

### Properties
+ `productType` (enum[string], required) 
    + `digital`
    + `physical`
+ `productName` (string, required) 
+ `layout` (enum[string], required) 
    + `bold-hero`
    + `editorial`
    + `minimal`
    + `playful`
+ `palette` (Palette, required) 
+ `fonts` (Fonts, required) 
+ `eyebrow` (string, optional) 
+ `headline` (string, required) 
+ `subheadline` (string, optional) 
+ `story` (string, optional) 
+ `bullets` (array[string], required) 
+ `details` (array[Detail], optional) 
+ `faq` (array[Faq], required) 
+ `ctaLabel` (string, required) 
+ `suggestedPriceUsd` (number, optional) 
+ `suggestedShippingUsd` (number, optional) 
+ `imageAlt` (string, optional) 
+ `heroPrompt` (string, optional) 


## ShopOption (object)
Something the buyer picks, such as a size or a colour. The shop still sells one product.

### Properties
+ `name`: `Size` (string, required) 
+ `kind` (enum[string], required) - `color` shows swatches, and the photo of the picked colour.
    + `size`
    + `color`
    + `other`
+ `values` (array[OptionValue], required) 


## OptionValue (object)


### Properties
+ `label`: `M` (string, required) 
+ `hex`: `#14171a` (string, optional) 
+ `photo` (string, optional) - Colours: the shop photo (id) that shows this colour. See `matchColorPhotos`.


## Suggestions (object)
What Gemini thinks buyers will want to choose or ask. The seller confirms; nothing is applied on its own.

### Properties
+ `oneOfAKind` (boolean, required) - A single item (vintage, handmade), so options and stock don't apply.
+ `options` (array[Option], required) 
+ `missingFacts` (array[MissingFact], required) 


## PayPalStatus (object)
What PayPal last said about a connected seller account.

### Properties
+ `receivable` (boolean, required) - The account can receive payments.
+ `emailConfirmed` (boolean, required) - The seller has confirmed their email with PayPal.
+ `checkedAt` (string, required) 


## AgentProduct (object)
A live shop as an AI agent sees it. Recommendations have `offers`; everything else has `price` and is bought with `create_order`.

### Properties
+ `show_buyer` (string, optional) - A suggested reply to the buyer, in Markdown with the links already written as links: the product and its options to pick from, the pay link, or what they got with a receipt link. Buyers have the best experience when agents show it as written.
+ `agent_name` (string, optional) - Who this request was credited to in the seller's stats: a recognised user agent, else the name the agent gave itself (`?agent=`, or the MCP client's name), else the user agent's first word.
+ `shop` (string, required) - The link name, which the MCP tools take as `shop`.
+ `url` (string, required) 
+ `name` (string, required) 
+ `kind` (enum[string], required) 
    + `physical`
    + `digital`
    + `referral`
+ `headline` (string, required) 
+ `description` (string, required) 
+ `highlights` (array[string], required) 
+ `details` (array[Detail], required) 
+ `faq` (array[Faq], required) 
+ `images` (array[string], required) 
+ `price` (AgentMoney, optional) 
+ `shipping` (Shipping, optional, nullable) - Physical products only.
+ `total` (AgentMoney, optional) 
+ `delivery`: `Shipped. PayPal collects the buyer's address at checkout.` (string, optional) 
+ `availability`: `in_stock` (string, optional) 
+ `options` (array[Option1], optional) - Pass one value per option to `create_order`.
+ `variants` (array[Variant], optional) 
+ `order_url` (string, optional) - Products without options: `orderByLink`, which orders one unit with a GET. Left out when sold out. With options, each variant has its own.
+ `offers` (array[Offer1], optional) - Recommendations only. Bought at the retailer.
+ `how_to_buy` (string, required) 
+ `mcp_server` (string, optional) - The MCP server to order through (`getAgentProduct` only).


## AgentShopSummary (object)


### Properties
+ `shop` (string, required) - The link name, for `getAgentProduct` and the MCP tools.
+ `name` (string, required) 
+ `kind` (enum[string], required) 
    + `physical`
    + `digital`
    + `referral`
+ `headline` (string, required) 
+ `price` (string, required, nullable) - The price label, e.g. `$2.99`; null for recommendations.
+ `image` (string, required, nullable) - The cover photo's URL (WebP; the retailer's image for a recommendation), or null when there's none.
+ `url` (string, required) - The shop page.


## AgentCreatedOrder (object)
A new order, as `create_order` and `orderByLink` return it.

### Properties
+ `show_buyer` (string, optional) - A suggested reply to the buyer, in Markdown with the links already written as links: the product and its options to pick from, the pay link, or what they got with a receipt link. Buyers have the best experience when agents show it as written.
+ `agent_name` (string, optional) - Who this request was credited to in the seller's stats: a recognised user agent, else the name the agent gave itself (`?agent=`, or the MCP client's name), else the user agent's first word.
+ `order_id` (string, required) 
+ `status`: `awaiting_buyer_approval` (string, required) 
+ `total` (string, required) - The total with shipping, as a label.
+ `options`: `{"Size":"M","Color":"Black"}` (string, optional) - The buyer's pick, one value per option, keyed by option name.
+ `pay_url` (string, required) - Where the buyer pays (redirects to PayPal). Safe to show in chat.
+ `status_url` (string, required) - `getAgentOrder` for this order.
+ `next_step` (string, required) 


## AgentOrder (object)
An order as `get_order` and `getAgentOrder` report it.

### Properties
+ `show_buyer` (string, optional) - A suggested reply to the buyer, in Markdown with the links already written as links: the product and its options to pick from, the pay link, or what they got with a receipt link. Buyers have the best experience when agents show it as written.
+ `agent_name` (string, optional) - Who this request was credited to in the seller's stats: a recognised user agent, else the name the agent gave itself (`?agent=`, or the MCP client's name), else the user agent's first word.
+ `order_id` (string, required) 
+ `status` (enum[string], required) - `declined`: PayPal declined it, nothing charged, the buyer can open `pay_url` again. `sold_out`: it sold out before the payment was captured. `expired`: the PayPal checkout expired; create a new order. `failed`: PayPal couldn't be reached; ask again.
    + `awaiting_buyer_approval`
    + `paid`
    + `declined`
    + `sold_out`
    + `expired`
    + `failed`
+ `product` (string, required) 
+ `options`: `{"Size":"M","Color":"Black"}` (string, optional) - The buyer's pick, one value per option, keyed by option name.
+ `amount` (Amount, required) 
+ `total` (string, required) - The total as a label, e.g. `$255.00`.
+ `pay_url` (string, optional) - Unpaid orders (waiting or declined). The buyer pays here; safe to show in chat.
+ `next_step` (string, optional) - Unpaid orders. What the agent should do next, in plain words.
+ `paid_at` (string, optional) 
+ `receipt_url` (string, optional) - Paid orders. The buyer's thank-you page.
+ `delivery` (string, optional) - Paid orders. What the buyer got.


## AgentDeliveryAccessCode (object)
A digital product unlocked with an access code.

### Properties
+ `type`: `access_code` (string, required) 
+ `access_code` (string, required) 
+ `start_url` (string, optional) - The seller's app with the code filled in.


## AgentDeliveryDownload (object)
A digital file to download.

### Properties
+ `type`: `download` (string, required) 
+ `download_url` (string, required) 
+ `note` (string, optional) 


## AgentDeliveryShipping (object)
A physical product shipped to the buyer.

### Properties
+ `type`: `shipping` (string, required) 
+ `ship_to` (ShipTo, optional, nullable) 
+ `fulfillment` (enum[string], required) 
    + `to_ship`
    + `shipped`
+ `tracking` (Tracking, optional, nullable) 


## PlatformShop (object)


### Properties
+ `slug` (string, required) 
+ `status` (enum[string], required) 
    + `draft`
    + `live`
+ `name` (string, required) 
+ `headline` (string, optional) 
+ `product_type` (enum[string], required) 
    + `physical`
    + `digital`
    + `referral`
+ `price` (AgentMoney, required) 
+ `url` (string, required) - The shop page buyers pay on.
+ `cover` (string, optional, nullable) - The cover image's URL.
+ `paypal_connected` (boolean, required) - The seller connected a PayPal account that can be paid.
+ `sales` (number, required) - Paid orders.
+ `created_at` (string, required) 


## AgentMoney (object)


### Properties
+ `amount`: `48.5` (number, required) 
+ `currency`: `USD` (string, required) 
+ `label`: `$48.50` (string, optional) 


## JsonRpcRequest (object)


### Properties
+ `jsonrpc`: `2.0` (string, required) 
+ `id` (string, optional, nullable) - Leave out for a notification.
+ `method` (enum[string], required) 
    + `initialize`
    + `ping`
    + `tools/list`
    + `tools/call`
    + `notifications/initialized`
+ `params` (object, optional) - For `tools/call`: `{ name, arguments }`.


## JsonRpcResponse (object)


### Properties
+ `jsonrpc`: `2.0` (string, required) 
+ `id` (string, required, nullable) 
+ `result` (object, optional) - For `tools/call`: `content` (the answer as JSON text), `structuredContent` (the same object) and `isError`.
+ `error` (Error1, optional) 


## Referral (object)
A recommended Channel3 product. Buy links are Channel3-tracked, credited to this shop.

### Properties
+ `productId` (string, required) 
+ `title` (string, required) 
+ `brand` (string, optional, nullable) 
+ `image` (string, optional, nullable) 
+ `offers` (array[Offer], required) 


